#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# inverse_fourier_transform

#% text
# `inverse_fourier_transform(g, w, t)` gives the inverse Fourier transform `1/sqrt(2 pi) integrate(g*exp(-im*w*t), [w, -inf, inf])` of `g`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# It is computed as `fourier_transform` is, with the opposite sign in the exponent.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# A Gaussian:

#% cell
inverse_fourier_transform(exp(-w^2/4)/sqrt(2), w, t)
#% output
#= exp(-t^2)

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# A band-limited spectrum:

#% cell
inverse_fourier_transform(unit_step(w + 1)*unit_step(1 - w), w, t)
#% output
#= (1/2)*(-1im*exp(1im*t)/t + 1im*exp(-1im*t)/t)*2^(1/2)*pi^(-1/2)

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The transform of the result is the spectrum:

#% cell
fourier_transform(inverse_fourier_transform(exp(-w^2), w, t), t, w)
#% output
#= exp(-w^2)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `fourier_transform`, `integrate`
